### Interactive & Reduced-Motion Contract

- **Play/Pause control:** `<button type="button" data-mech-toggle aria-pressed="false">` (`>= 44×44px` hit target, visible `:focus-visible` ring) toggles `data-paused="true"` on `.mech-figure`, sets `animation-play-state: paused` on all `.signal-stream` and `.signal-node-pulse` elements, calls `svg.pauseAnimations()` / `svg.unpauseAnimations()` when available, and announces the state via `aria-live="polite"`.
- **Keyboard stage inspection:** Users can step through `All stages`, `1. Auth Request`, `2. Auth Code`, and `3. Token Exchange` via the control buttons or by focusing and pressing `Enter` / `Space` (`Escape` to reset) on any SVG stage pill; non-active stages dim to `0.55` opacity (never hidden) and the `aria-live="polite"` caption describes the active step.
- **Reduced motion (`@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)`):** Disables all continuous `stroke-dashoffset` and pulse animations (`animation: none !important; animation-play-state: paused !important;`), initializes the toggle to its paused state on load, and keeps directional `<marker>` arrowheads, tracks, and numbered stage badges (`1`, `2`, `3`) at full static clarity.

